<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  DRAFT FOR REVIEW. Not installed, not loaded. Installing it is Duho's call.
  Written 2026-08-26.

  Note on style: flag names below are written without their leading dashes,
  because an XML comment may not contain a double hyphen. The first draft of
  this file spelled them normally and was malformed XML as a result; plutil
  lint accepted it and a real parser did not.

  Why it exists: the provider usage monitor had no launcher at all. It was last
  started by hand, stopped at some point, and the cockpit usage panel sat on a
  held-over 85 percent for two days before Duho noticed the number never moved.

  Shape follows com.nebulamind.cockpit-render: StartInterval plus a single-pass
  invocation, NOT the script's watch mode. launchd owns the cadence, so a
  crashed or killed pass costs one interval instead of stopping updates for
  good, and no long-lived process is left to leak. The script exits after one
  pass when watch mode is absent, which is what makes this work.

  Interval is 300 seconds deliberately, not the script's 60 second default. The
  Claude OAuth read is cached for 15 minutes and backs off an hour on HTTP 429,
  but Moonshot and Nous are queried on every pass. Polling once a minute is what
  earned the 429 that broke this panel; five minutes is ample for a quota bar.

  The refresh-slash option is deliberately not passed. It drives visible slash
  commands inside agent panes, and a scheduled job should never type into a
  coordinator's session unattended.

  PATH is set explicitly because launchd does not inherit a login shell's. The
  first install failed on its very first run with FileNotFoundError: 'tmux' —
  the monitor shells out to tmux, which lives in /opt/homebrew/bin, and launchd
  starts with a minimal PATH that does not include it. It tested clean by hand
  only because an interactive shell had the full PATH.

  To install, after review:
    cp tools/cockpit-scheduling/com.nebulamind.provider-usage-monitor.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nebulamind.provider-usage-monitor.plist
  To stop and remove:
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nebulamind.provider-usage-monitor.plist
    rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nebulamind.provider-usage-monitor.plist

  Before loading: a hand-started watch-mode process has been running at 5 minute
  intervals since 2026-08-26 16:24. Kill it first, or both will write and
  contend for the stable_cockpit_guard single-writer lock.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.nebulamind.provider-usage-monitor</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/Users/duhokim/NebulaMind/NebulaMind/tools/live_provider_usage_monitor.py</string>
        <string>--interval</string>
        <string>300</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/duhokim/NebulaMind/NebulaMind</string>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/duhokim/HermesOps/cockpit/provider-usage-launchd.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/duhokim/HermesOps/cockpit/provider-usage-launchd.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
